# Dotfiles .gitignore
#
# NOTE: tracked config lives under home/ and legitimately starts with a dot
# (home/.config, home/.agents, ...). Do NOT add blanket rules like `.*` — they
# would ignore the very dotfiles this repo exists to track. Ignore only cruft,
# machine-local overrides, and — most importantly — secrets.

# ─── Secrets & credentials (never commit) ───────────────────────────
# SSH / GPG / TLS keys
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*_rsa
*_ed25519
# Known secret-bearing files
.netrc
.pgpass
**/.aws/credentials
**/.ssh/known_hosts
**/*secret*
**/*credentials*
**/*.token
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ─── Tool configs that embed tokens (never track, even if the tool ──
#     dir is otherwise stowed — track the sibling non-secret config only)
# NOTE: .gitignore has no inline comments — a trailing `#` is part of the
# pattern, not a comment. Both rules below carried one and therefore matched
# nothing, silently, for as long as they have existed. Keep comments on their
# own line.
# GitHub CLI OAuth token (only absent today because macOS keychains it)
**/gh/hosts.yml
**/github-copilot/apps.json
# 1Password CLI account config
**/op/config
**/.config/fabric/.env

# ─── Machine-local overrides (per-host, not shared) ─────────────────
*.local
**/*.local.*
home*/.config/**/local.*
*.private
# ...but the XDG ~/.local dir is NOT a machine-local override — keep it tracked
!home*/.local/
!home*/.local/**

# ─── Package/tooling artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.npm/
*.log
# Installer-managed binary (currently >100 MB; GitHub rejects files over 100 MB)
home*/.local/bin/plannotator

# ─── Editors / IDEs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ─── OS cruft ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db

# ─── Fisher-managed fish plugin files ───────────────────────────────
#     Derived from home/.config/fish/fish_plugins; restored with `fisher update`.
#     We track our OWN config.fish + conf.d/*.fish + fish_plugins, not these.
#
#     `home*/` throughout this file: rules must cover the shared tree AND the
#     platform overlays, or a file stops being ignored the moment it moves.
home*/.config/fish/functions/*
home*/.config/fish/completions/*
home*/.config/fish/conf.d/git.fish
# ...but keep the fish files we author ourselves. Generated tool completions
# (docker/kubectl/orb/orbctl) stay ignored — `dotfiles fish` regenerates them,
# `dotfiles doctor` verifies them.
!home*/.config/fish/completions/dotfiles.fish
!home*/.config/fish/functions/theme_gruvbox.fish
!home*/.config/fish/functions/open.fish
# fish's universal variable store — holds this machine's resolved fish_user_paths.
home*/.config/fish/fish_variables

# ─── Pi agent config ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#     Web access cache and credentials are machine-local runtime state.
home*/.pi/web-search-cache/
home*/.pi/web-search.json
#     Ignore all of agent/ by default (auth.json holds secrets, sessions/ is
#     runtime state), then un-ignore only what we author: settings, themes,
#     and extension config. auth.json + sessions/ stay LOCAL and uncommitted.
home*/.pi/agent/*
!home*/.pi/agent/settings.json
!home*/.pi/agent/themes/
!home*/.pi/agent/extensions/
home*/.pi/agent/extensions/*
!home*/.pi/agent/extensions/zed.ts
!home*/.pi/agent/extensions/subagent/
!home*/.pi/agent/extensions/subagent/config.json
# NOTE: skills/ is intentionally NOT tracked here — Pi consumes the canonical pool from
# the skills repo via ~/.pi/agent/skills -> ~/.agents/skills (see `dotfiles skills`).

# ─── Claude Code config ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#     ~/.claude is Claude Code's runtime home — auth, sessions, history,
#     projects/ (tens of MB), plugin caches. We author exactly one file there.
#     Same shape as the Pi and Zed blocks: deny by default, un-ignore what we
#     author. On a machine where ~/.claude does not exist yet, stow FOLDS the
#     directory (one link to the whole package), so Claude Code then writes all
#     of that state straight into the repo — these rules keep it out of git.
#     The `skills` link inside it is placed by `dotfiles skills`, not by stow.
home*/.claude/*
!home*/.claude/settings.json

# ─── Zed config ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#     stow FOLDS this directory (~/.config/zed is one symlink to the whole
#     package, not a link per file), so Zed writes its runtime state straight
#     into the repo — prompts/ is an LMDB database + lock file, not config.
#     Same shape as the Pi block above: deny by default, un-ignore what we author.
home*/.config/zed/*
!home*/.config/zed/settings.json
!home*/.config/zed/keymap.json
!home*/.config/zed/AGENTS.md
!home*/.config/zed/themes/

# ─── Stow / install runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Backups the install script makes before replacing a real dir/symlink.
*.bak
*.bak.*
